Blackdrift: give Glean no network uploader and never start usage reporting.

Why: 0100-0102 switch telemetry off through flags (Glean uploadEnabled =
false, the two usage pings disabled, no crash services, no Nimbus server),
but Glean still holds a working HTTP uploader. Any ping that does not follow
the upload flag would still be sent through it: the usage-reporting and
usage-deletion-request pings (follows_collection_enabled: false, kept off
only by setEnabled(false) in 0100), Glean's built-in deletion-request ping,
and any such ping a future upstream or library pings.yaml adds. This patch
closes the transport itself:

- Glean gets NoUploadPingUploader, which never opens a connection and
  answers every ping with Incapable, so Glean drops it. Nothing Glean
  records can leave the device, whatever a ping's flags say.
- the usage-reporting service is never started at launch, and
  Settings.isDailyUsagePingEnabled is always false, so a value stored by an
  older build is ignored and no usage profile id is generated.
- DailyUsageReportingSwitchPreference, the only other caller of the
  service's start(), is deleted; 0100 already removed it from the settings
  screen.
- Nimbus is created with no endpoint URL even when a .nimbus file exists at
  build time (0101 already removes its server settings and the fetch).

Covered already and unchanged here: crash upload and the send-report box
(0102), the Data choices and Crashes settings (0100, 0102), and the Nimbus
experiment fetch (0101).

Cut against: mozilla-firefox/firefox@6181e6b5f28a8fbae1d5c3ef6f6626b5a2180213 (Firefox 159.0.1).

